LibertinusSerif-Regular.otf and DejaVuSansMono.ttf are the same files
already embedded in smaragd via typst-kit's `embedded-fonts` feature (used
for print-PDF export — see `export::style`), copied here as standalone
files so they can also be registered directly with egui for on-screen use
in the Editor and Preview (see `src/editor_font.rs`). No additional
license terms apply for those two beyond what's already accepted by
depending on typst-kit/typst-assets with that feature enabled.

AtkinsonHyperlegible-Regular.ttf is *not* part of typst-kit's embedded set
— it's bundled independently and registered with both egui (via
`editor_font::install`) and the Typst PDF compiler directly (via
`TypstEngine::builder().fonts(...)` in `export::pdf`) so styles naming it
render identically in Preview and PDF, the same guarantee the other two
fonts have.

